        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Only a small amount of oxygen remains dissolved in plasma. Most enters red blood cells and binds reversibly to hemoglobin. This transport system greatly increases how much oxygen the blood can carry. Oxygenated blood then returns to the heart and is pumped through the systemic circulation."
