        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Active tissues consume oxygen during cellular respiration, lowering oxygen partial pressure around their cells. That gradient favors oxygen leaving the blood, separating from hemoglobin, and diffusing into tissue. The complete path is driven by linked gradients: ventilation refreshes alveolar air, circulation moves blood, and metabolism maintains demand."
        },
